  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 134 PM CDT Thu Oct 15 2026\n\nThe weekend is shaping up to be rather cool, with high pressure \nsettling in and temperatures in the 60s and lower 70s on Saturday. \nSaturday night will be even colder than Friday night, as strong \nradiational cooling sends temperatures down in the lower to middle \n40s over the Hill Country and Edwards Plateau, and into the mid to \nupper 40s elsewhere. 850mb temperatures will even dip as low as 2 to \n3 C Saturday morning, which is fairly impressive given how warm its \nbeen lately. \n\nOn Sunday, we start to see surface flow and return flow develop out \nof the east and southeast, particularly late in the day, but highs \nwill still only climb into the 60s and 70s. The slow and steady \nwarming trend continues Monday through the middle to end of next \nweek, but there are signs of increased rainfall towards late week \nand next weekend. For now, things are dry after the passage of this \nfront through the middle of next week.",
